cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Local LLMs for Bioinformatics: a three-environment benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Five open-weights language models (Qwen3.5-122B-A10B, Qwen3.5-35B-A3B, gpt-oss-20b,
  Qwen3.5-9B, Gemma-4-E4B) answered 53 automatically scored bioinformatics items
  (executed scripts, lab calculations, and tool/gene facts with and without
  retrieval-augmented generation) on a laptop, an Azure T4 VM and RTU HPC L40S nodes,
  using the same llama.cpp build. Includes frozen inputs, raw per-item results,
  scoring code and infrastructure code to reproduce the runs.
authors:
  - name: "MedicalEnvironment"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MedicalEnvironment/comperehensive_llm_run"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - large language models
  - benchmark
  - llama.cpp
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - HPC
  - Azure
